{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261004T014539Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "d43d2f13301d3339cfd26d87", "title": "[AINews] not much happened today", "url": "https://www.latent.space/p/ainews-not-much-happened-today-cee", "source": "Latent.Space", "published": "2026-10-03T08:45:15+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.77, "worthiness_confidence": 0.85, "final_score": 0.77, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "feed_full_text", "text_chars": 36963, "delivered": true, "summary": "OpenAI released GPT-6.1 Sol at $2/$10 per million tokens—39% cheaper than GPT-6 Sol while scoring 1.52 points higher on benchmarks. Anthropic's Sonnet 5.5 debuted at #3 on Agent Arena. These pricing shifts reshape cost-performance tradeoffs for builders choosing between frontier models. Key takeaway: Sol's efficiency gains and Sonnet's strong performance suggest the frontier is consolidating around two providers with distinct positioning—cheap-and-fast versus premium-reasoning—making model selection increasingly about workload fit rather than raw capability.", "jev_ms": 623.2, "jev_input_tokens": 9968, "jev_cost": 0.000418656, "llm_ms": 3248.8, "llm_cost": 0.010822, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261004T014539Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "bd1136d0fcfd6f1357de280a", "title": "The Agent Said It Was Done. The Database Disagreed.", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/microsoft/thinkingbox", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-03T22:56:48+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.985, "worthiness_confidence": 0.95, "final_score": 0.985, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 19251, "delivered": true, "summary": "Microsoft and Hugging Face released ThinkingBox, a benchmark that evaluates AI agents on actual database state changes rather than tool calls alone. Across 507 stateful business workflows run 20 times each, 67% of failures still invoked tools correctly but left wrong field values or missing effects. Claude Opus 5.5 leads at 67.16% pass@1 but only 47.53% pass@20, while Kimi-K3 solves 93.89% of tasks at least once but just 13.41% consistently. For production agents, consistency matters more than single-attempt accuracy—GPT-5.4 costs $6.80 per dependable task versus $0.131 per successful attempt. The key insight: verify terminal database state before committing, not the model's summary.", "jev_ms": 299.1, "jev_input_tokens": 6396, "jev_cost": 0.000268632, "llm_ms": 4259.9, "llm_cost": 0.007027, "errors": []}
